1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,660
I swear, milady, I will
not let you down! Huh?

2
00:00:05,020 --> 00:00:07,440
I am resolute and energized!

3
00:00:07,940 --> 00:00:11,060
I am motivated and I am invincible!

4
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:16,580
System Call!

5
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:22,560
Generate Thermal Element!

6
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:37,100
Oh, my God.

7
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:55,500
It's a strong hope to shine

8
00:00:57,460 --> 00:01:00,420
Come on, let's go

9
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:03,917
I've hidden voices in the

10
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:08,817
voice of your voice I've

11
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:10,937
never been told that you were

12
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:04,980
Ah, the sound of your voice will be heard

13
00:02:06,020 --> 00:02:08,860
I'll continue to fight with my luck

14
00:02:11,380 --> 00:02:14,480
Back of my soul, ah

15
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:41,340
I had no idea he could
conjure such spells.

16
00:02:41,780 --> 00:02:43,380
I underestimated him.

17
00:02:44,280 --> 00:02:47,440
That fire giant is a being
made entirely of magic.

18
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:50,140
My flowers cannot destroy such a thing,

19
00:02:50,340 --> 00:02:53,037
and I doubt they could
hold it off for very long.

20
00:02:53,120 --> 00:02:53,950
How long?

21
00:02:54,140 --> 00:02:58,217
I mean, we don't need that much time,
just enough to get up close to Chudelkin.

22
00:02:58,300 --> 00:03:00,640
For ten seconds. No more.

23
00:03:00,900 --> 00:03:02,320
Perhaps less than that.

24
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:03,936
Still, you're right.

25
00:03:04,380 --> 00:03:06,792
I'll draw its attention while you attack.

26
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:09,300
But do not advance too far.

27
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:12,312
That is what the Pontifex is waiting for.

28
00:03:12,980 --> 00:03:14,300
Ten seconds?

29
00:03:29,820 --> 00:03:31,740
Swarm my flowers!

30
00:04:09,060 --> 00:04:11,440
Go for her eyes. You got it.

31
00:04:12,200 --> 00:04:13,160
System call.

32
00:04:14,960 --> 00:04:15,790
Discharge!

33
00:04:17,440 --> 00:04:18,340
No, no, no, no!

34
00:04:18,540 --> 00:04:20,011
Watch out, you residents!

35
00:04:26,540 --> 00:04:27,580
What's he doing?

36
00:04:30,020 --> 00:04:31,420
No!

37
00:04:40,300 --> 00:04:41,700
No!

38
00:04:43,580 --> 00:04:44,410
Huh?

39
00:04:48,060 --> 00:04:49,460
Ahhh!

40
00:04:59,360 --> 00:05:00,760
Your...

41
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:04,300
M &M's...

42
00:05:19,580 --> 00:05:20,410
Kirito...

43
00:05:25,280 --> 00:05:28,040
Well, that was rather anticlimactic.

44
00:05:28,400 --> 00:05:32,940
I did gain some useful information from
it, though, so it's not a total loss.

45
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:35,440
How unsightly.

46
00:05:39,900 --> 00:05:41,040
Heartless creature!

47
00:05:41,420 --> 00:05:46,280
So, irregular boy, I think I've
figured out the mystery of you.

48
00:05:47,660 --> 00:05:52,700
At first, I thought I couldn't see your
properties because you were unregistered.

49
00:05:52,900 --> 00:05:54,680
An illegitimate birth.

50
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:56,157
But I was wrong.

51
00:05:56,240 --> 00:05:57,280
You're human.

52
00:05:57,540 --> 00:05:58,760
Not from this world.

53
00:05:59,020 --> 00:06:00,417
You're from the other side.

54
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:01,420
Aren't you?

55
00:06:02,840 --> 00:06:03,860
I am.

56
00:06:09,700 --> 00:06:10,560
So what?

57
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:13,273
You don't feel threatened by me, do you?

58
00:06:13,400 --> 00:06:15,897
I got the same authority
level as everyone else.

59
00:06:15,980 --> 00:06:19,417
It's nowhere near as high as yours,
that's for sure, Administrator.

60
00:06:19,500 --> 00:06:20,640
Sorry, Queen Nella.

61
00:06:23,220 --> 00:06:24,580
Oh, that little imp.

62
00:06:24,820 --> 00:06:27,357
She's filled your head
with ridiculous stories.

63
00:06:27,440 --> 00:06:30,860
Well, boy, what are you doing in my world?

64
00:06:31,060 --> 00:06:33,766
I doubt you just stumbled
in out of curiosity.

65
00:06:33,860 --> 00:06:35,137
You're right, I didn't.

66
00:06:35,220 --> 00:06:39,300
Your world's gonna end real soon,
and it's gonna be all your fault.

67
00:06:39,720 --> 00:06:41,060
I'm sorry, what?

68
00:06:41,440 --> 00:06:44,980
Are you saying I'll
destroy it? Pretty much.

69
00:06:45,240 --> 00:06:47,160
The Dark Territory will invade.

70
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:50,617
That's why you made the
Integrity Knights, to stop it.

71
00:06:50,700 --> 00:06:52,935
But your faith in them's your mistake.

72
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:54,660
They won't be enough.

73
00:06:55,560 --> 00:06:59,207
That sounds exactly like something
that little brat would say.

74
00:06:59,700 --> 00:07:00,580
How pitiful.

75
00:07:00,900 --> 00:07:06,500
Both her for being so desperate to have me
expelled, and you for being so gullible.

76
00:07:06,820 --> 00:07:08,640
Madam Pontifex, if I may.

77
00:07:09,180 --> 00:07:11,660
The army of the Dark has grown rapidly.

78
00:07:12,060 --> 00:07:15,957
If they invade now, the current
number of knights cannot withstand it.

79
00:07:16,040 --> 00:07:17,780
The commander believed so.

80
00:07:18,240 --> 00:07:20,480
As did Vice Commander Fanatio.

81
00:07:20,880 --> 00:07:21,800
And I.

82
00:07:22,060 --> 00:07:23,120
I as well.

83
00:07:23,720 --> 00:07:26,757
What is your plan now that the
Order of Knights is no more?

84
00:07:26,840 --> 00:07:29,546
Do you think you alone
can protect the Empire?

85
00:07:30,300 --> 00:07:32,840
But what angers me more than your hubris?

86
00:07:33,160 --> 00:07:37,680
You have stolen us knights from our
parents, from wives and husbands,

87
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:39,480
brothers and sisters.

88
00:07:39,980 --> 00:07:43,597
You sealed away our memories
of them and replaced them

89
00:07:43,680 --> 00:07:46,915
with lies of being summoned
from a non-existent heaven.

90
00:07:48,860 --> 00:07:53,507
Pontifex, could you not trust us to be
loyal to you and respect your authority?

91
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:55,477
Were we such a threat to you?

92
00:07:55,560 --> 00:08:01,520
You had to submit us to such a monstrous
ritual and force our souls into obedience?

93
00:08:06,060 --> 00:08:07,980
I do trust you, though.

94
00:08:08,460 --> 00:08:09,940
In fact, I love you.

95
00:08:10,460 --> 00:08:14,220
The piety module installed in
Unites is proof of my love.

96
00:08:14,420 --> 00:08:16,420
A gift from me to you all.

97
00:08:16,740 --> 00:08:20,975
Why, this little thing frees you from
the worry and pain of normal folk.

98
00:08:21,280 --> 00:08:25,340
You are my beautiful dolls,
beautiful for all eternity.

99
00:08:26,400 --> 00:08:32,020
Out of all the knights, uncle, Commander
Bercouli has shown you the deepest loyalty.

100
00:08:32,680 --> 00:08:34,720
But you do not know the man,

101
00:08:34,940 --> 00:08:39,600
even though he has served you
faithfully for 300 long years.

102
00:08:40,900 --> 00:08:44,180
Do you think he did not
suffer once in all that time?

103
00:08:44,420 --> 00:08:47,538
Did you not know of the pain
he carried in his heart?

104
00:08:47,640 --> 00:08:49,540
Are you that oblivious?

105
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:53,640
You think so little of me.

106
00:08:53,860 --> 00:08:55,020
Of course I knew.

107
00:08:55,560 --> 00:08:59,597
These things you speak of didn't start
bothering Bercouli recently, though.

108
00:08:59,680 --> 00:09:01,500
He brought them up ages ago.

109
00:09:01,700 --> 00:09:02,900
A century, I think?

110
00:09:03,220 --> 00:09:04,985
Yes, about that, give or take.

111
00:09:05,100 --> 00:09:07,897
I couldn't watch him brood
over such trivialities.

112
00:09:07,980 --> 00:09:09,160
So I fixed him.

113
00:09:09,560 --> 00:09:11,384
Reset him, to be more specific.

114
00:09:13,140 --> 00:09:15,080
And he was not the only one.

115
00:09:15,380 --> 00:09:18,520
I reset every night
more than a century old.

116
00:09:18,760 --> 00:09:22,819
All of their painful memories and
troubling thoughts were wiped away.

117
00:09:23,220 --> 00:09:24,800
Don't you worry, Alice.

118
00:09:25,340 --> 00:09:27,917
I'll overlook your
transgressions and erase

119
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:30,137
all the thoughts that
make you so miserable,

120
00:09:30,220 --> 00:09:31,050
too.

121
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:36,026
Before you know it, you'll go back to
being my puppet and have no need to think.

122
00:09:38,820 --> 00:09:40,000
You are correct.

123
00:09:40,460 --> 00:09:44,880
Right now, I feel enough sadness
and pain to tear my heart to pieces.

124
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:48,460
However, I choose to embrace it.

125
00:09:49,300 --> 00:09:52,557
I do not wish to erase what
I have never felt before.

126
00:09:52,640 --> 00:09:55,520
This pain serves a purpose.

127
00:09:55,940 --> 00:09:57,760
It reminds me what I am.

128
00:09:58,180 --> 00:10:00,980
A human being and not a puppet knight.

129
00:10:02,160 --> 00:10:08,960
Madam Pontifex, I do not want your so-called
love, and I do not need you to fix me!

130
00:10:09,320 --> 00:10:10,980
I'm sad to hear that.

131
00:10:11,460 --> 00:10:14,048
Unfortunately, what you
want doesn't matter.

132
00:10:14,220 --> 00:10:16,900
As soon as I resynthesize you, and I will,

133
00:10:17,140 --> 00:10:21,060
the pesky feelings that trouble
you now will be erased completely.

134
00:10:22,500 --> 00:10:26,441
Kind of like what you did to yourself
way back when, huh, Quinella?

135
00:10:27,440 --> 00:10:28,880
Watch it, little boy.

136
00:10:29,320 --> 00:10:32,900
Dredging up the past is
considered quite rude. Why?

137
00:10:33,200 --> 00:10:35,259
You scared the truth will come out?

138
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:38,240
No one's got the power to erase the past.

139
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:39,440
Not even you.

140
00:10:39,860 --> 00:10:44,437
You were born a human and raised a human,
and no matter how much power you got,

141
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:47,277
that's one thing you
can't change, can you?

142
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:52,600
I'm not quite sure what you're getting
at, little boy from the outer world.

143
00:10:52,840 --> 00:10:57,369
All you want is to be a god, but you
can never be a god because you're human.

144
00:10:58,360 --> 00:11:02,700
Being human means you make
mistakes, and you made a big one.

145
00:11:02,940 --> 00:11:05,999
At this point, there's
nothing you can do to fix it.

146
00:11:06,300 --> 00:11:08,700
You got less Integrity Knights now.

147
00:11:08,980 --> 00:11:12,274
If the Dark Territory invades,
who's going to stop them?

148
00:11:12,460 --> 00:11:14,048
They'll destroy everything.

149
00:11:14,420 --> 00:11:17,617
And who was the one who corrupted
some of my best knights?

150
00:11:17,700 --> 00:11:19,160
That was you, boy.

151
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:24,297
If you're all that's left after this, maybe
you can start over with a clean slate.

152
00:11:24,380 --> 00:11:26,417
Maybe that's what you always wanted.

153
00:11:26,500 --> 00:11:29,324
Thing is, it ain't gonna
go the way you want it.

154
00:11:29,820 --> 00:11:31,140
On the other side,

155
00:11:31,240 --> 00:11:33,157
there's the people who created this world

156
00:11:33,240 --> 00:11:35,557
and have final say over
what happens to it.

157
00:11:35,640 --> 00:11:40,720
When they see the human empire fall,
they'll think, Oh well, that didn't work.

158
00:11:40,860 --> 00:11:42,077
I guess we'll start over.

159
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:46,336
And then, one of them will push a
button and everything will disappear.

160
00:11:47,020 --> 00:11:47,850
The mountains.

161
00:11:48,100 --> 00:11:49,160
The rivers.

162
00:11:51,360 --> 00:11:52,460
The towns.

163
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:57,720
Every person here and you.

164
00:11:58,020 --> 00:12:00,608
They'll erase it all
in the blink of an eye.

165
00:12:04,100 --> 00:12:05,340
Point taken.

166
00:12:05,840 --> 00:12:09,160
But I have a feeling the
same goes for your world too.

167
00:12:09,620 --> 00:12:11,257
You must have a creator.

168
00:12:11,340 --> 00:12:13,657
Does your kind grapple with the thought of

169
00:12:13,740 --> 00:12:16,557
living under the whim of
a higher power as well?

170
00:12:16,640 --> 00:12:18,900
Do you strive to please this being,

171
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:23,120
obeying its laws, hoping it won't
tire of you and wipe you out?

172
00:12:24,940 --> 00:12:27,640
I would be shocked if that were the case.

173
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:29,600
As you say,

174
00:12:29,840 --> 00:12:33,240
your kind created our
world, and if we fail them,

175
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:35,518
they would delete us without a care.

176
00:12:36,040 --> 00:12:39,000
If that is how your kind treat us, boy,

177
00:12:39,340 --> 00:12:42,105
then you do not have the
right to criticize me.

178
00:12:42,360 --> 00:12:44,300
I reject their authority.

179
00:12:45,540 --> 00:12:48,177
I will not pander to self-proclaimed gods

180
00:12:48,260 --> 00:12:51,020
groveling for the right
to continue existing.

181
00:12:51,460 --> 00:12:53,080
I refute them all.

182
00:12:53,280 --> 00:12:57,860
I exist for one reason alone,
to rule over all in this world.

183
00:12:58,160 --> 00:13:02,317
That singular desire is what
drives me and gives me life.

184
00:13:02,400 --> 00:13:05,920
My legs are for climbing over
others to greater heights,

185
00:13:06,220 --> 00:13:08,780
not to bend at the knee in subjugation!

186
00:13:11,220 --> 00:13:12,400
And then what?

187
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:16,620
Are you gonna sit back and let
the human empire get destroyed?

188
00:13:17,120 --> 00:13:19,340
Are you gonna watch everything burn?

189
00:13:19,500 --> 00:13:21,140
Alone on your token throne?

190
00:13:21,320 --> 00:13:22,967
a queen with no one to rule?

191
00:13:23,480 --> 00:13:28,480
On the contrary, I will not allow
your kind to reset the underworld,

192
00:13:28,920 --> 00:13:31,177
nor will I allow the final load test?

193
00:13:31,260 --> 00:13:32,731
to run its course either.

194
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:36,380
I've prepared a new sacred
art to counter that, in fact.

195
00:13:37,200 --> 00:13:38,380
So be honored.

196
00:13:38,820 --> 00:13:42,420
You will be witnesses, the
first to test my creation.

197
00:13:42,880 --> 00:13:44,120
What creation?

198
00:13:45,200 --> 00:13:49,920
The Knights were a stopgap, and
they have served their purpose well.

199
00:13:50,420 --> 00:13:55,200
The military force I require should
not think, or feel, or remember.

200
00:13:55,460 --> 00:13:57,237
In battle, those are distractions.

201
00:13:57,320 --> 00:14:03,660
My perfect soldier relentlessly massacres
whatever enemy stands before it.

202
00:14:04,700 --> 00:14:08,040
Ultimately, what I require is not human.

203
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:13,920
Wake and destroy your
enemy, my faithful servant,

204
00:14:14,380 --> 00:14:16,220
my soulless exterminator!

205
00:14:16,720 --> 00:14:18,500
Release Recollection!

206
00:14:21,240 --> 00:14:23,300
What's she done? Impossible!

207
00:14:39,800 --> 00:14:41,200
Discharge!

208
00:15:15,040 --> 00:15:16,460
This can't be.

209
00:15:16,960 --> 00:15:18,480
All those weapons?

210
00:15:19,700 --> 00:15:23,465
Using perfect weapon control in
30 at once should be impossible.

211
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:25,217
Even for the Pontifex.

212
00:15:25,300 --> 00:15:27,380
It violates the sacred arts.

213
00:15:31,840 --> 00:15:35,100
At long last, the power I have sought.

214
00:15:35,680 --> 00:15:37,580
Offensive might with no equal.

215
00:15:37,800 --> 00:15:39,800
A soldier that will fight forever.

216
00:15:40,320 --> 00:15:42,940
Now, what shall I call it?

217
00:15:43,540 --> 00:15:44,600
I know.

218
00:15:45,040 --> 00:15:46,760
The Sword Golem.

219
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:50,340
No way.

220
00:15:50,620 --> 00:15:52,340
It's a walking sword.

221
00:15:58,640 --> 00:16:02,960
Each one of its blades has the
priority level of a divine object.

222
00:16:03,320 --> 00:16:07,780
I stretched my precious memory
capacity to the limit to create this,

223
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,620
the ultimate weapon.

224
00:16:10,140 --> 00:16:12,360
Do you think you can defeat it?

225
00:16:17,940 --> 00:16:20,520
Now, go forth and fight, my golem!

226
00:16:21,120 --> 00:16:23,200
Go and annihilate your enemies!

227
00:16:32,700 --> 00:16:34,100
Oh.

228
00:16:43,380 --> 00:16:45,280
That's all.

229
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:48,020
Oh. Oh.

230
00:16:49,420 --> 00:16:50,250
Oh.

231
00:16:50,560 --> 00:16:51,390
Oh.

232
00:16:57,960 --> 00:16:59,360
Uh…

233
00:17:01,420 --> 00:17:02,820
Uh…

234
00:17:06,300 --> 00:17:07,617
Uh…

235
00:17:07,700 --> 00:17:09,180
Ah!

236
00:17:10,060 --> 00:17:10,890
Ah!

237
00:17:13,120 --> 00:17:14,520
Uh…

238
00:17:17,900 --> 00:17:18,730
Ah…

239
00:17:19,300 --> 00:17:20,130
Ah!

240
00:17:40,340 --> 00:17:41,260
Yew-Gio!

241
00:17:41,380 --> 00:17:42,460
Use your dagger!

242
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:45,680
Stab the levitating disc!

243
00:17:46,740 --> 00:17:48,280
I'll buy you some time.

244
00:17:49,140 --> 00:17:49,970
Hurry!

245
00:18:13,540 --> 00:18:15,720
Oh, my God.

246
00:18:36,700 --> 00:18:39,580
Thank goodness, he made it.

247
00:18:43,000 --> 00:18:49,880
I'm happy I got to fight
with you one last time.

248
00:19:17,940 --> 00:19:20,540
Oh, my God.

249
00:19:20,940 --> 00:19:24,540
Oh, my God.

250
00:19:56,360 --> 00:19:58,800
Kirito, who is this person?

251
00:19:59,260 --> 00:20:00,220
She's Cardinal.

252
00:20:00,920 --> 00:20:03,180
She's the good pontifex of this world.

253
00:20:03,980 --> 00:20:08,627
Two hundred years ago, she fought
Administrator, but she had to go into hiding.

254
00:20:08,980 --> 00:20:12,340
She saved Eugeo and me and
guided us into the cathedral.

255
00:20:12,680 --> 00:20:13,880
She wants to help.

256
00:20:14,100 --> 00:20:16,335
No one loves this world more than her.

257
00:20:16,760 --> 00:20:18,080
I don't doubt it.

258
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:20,920
I trust the warmth of her power.

259
00:20:21,200 --> 00:20:23,220
Thank you for healing me, m 'lady.

260
00:20:36,820 --> 00:20:38,360
You stubborn fool.

261
00:20:38,700 --> 00:20:40,876
Did I not relieve you of your duties?

262
00:20:41,320 --> 00:20:44,040
Did I not thank you
for all your hard work?

263
00:20:44,520 --> 00:20:47,167
Why couldn't you just
stay on your bookshelf?

264
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:48,910
I'm sorry.

265
00:20:49,220 --> 00:20:51,040
Did she have a Fluctlight too?

266
00:20:52,860 --> 00:20:53,690
No.

267
00:20:53,773 --> 00:20:57,160
To borrow a term from your
world, Charlotte was like an NPC.

268
00:20:57,620 --> 00:20:58,680
Wait, what?

269
00:20:58,960 --> 00:21:00,217
But she...

270
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:02,620
she risked her life to save me.

271
00:21:03,500 --> 00:21:05,900
That's not something an NPC'd do.

272
00:21:06,180 --> 00:21:09,297
I mean, if she didn't have a soul, then...

273
00:21:09,380 --> 00:21:12,380
This child had been alive for 200 years.

274
00:21:13,360 --> 00:21:18,740
She was my constant companion, and she
watched over a number of people for me.

275
00:21:19,720 --> 00:21:22,600
For the past two years, she was with you.

276
00:21:23,300 --> 00:21:28,560
After spending all that time with someone,
one doesn't need a Fluctlight to care.

277
00:21:29,840 --> 00:21:35,480
Even if the nature of an intelligence is
just a collection of input and output data,

278
00:21:35,780 --> 00:21:39,140
it is still possible for it
to have a true soul within.

279
00:21:39,960 --> 00:21:42,740
and in some cases, love.

280
00:21:43,900 --> 00:21:47,120
A concept you'll never
understand as long as you live!

281
00:21:48,140 --> 00:21:50,760
Administrator, you wretched woman!

282
00:22:53,280 --> 00:22:57,220
Thank you so much for watching.

283
00:23:11,493 --> 00:23:13,217
And everything turns to dust to dust

284
00:23:35,920 --> 00:23:38,620
Next time, Administrator.
